{
    "comment": [
        "REY_PLL digital blocks, ciccreator object file compiled with",
        "cicpy (cd work && make cic, through cic/ip.json). The cells are rey_tr standard",
        "cells read from the built REY_TR_SKY130A library; routes are by",
        "net name, no coordinates. Ported from sun_pll's SUN_PLL.json.",
        "",
        "Routing rules for rey_tr columns, learned on REY_PLL_CTRL (clean):",
        " - a cell's output Y lies under its own VSS strip on M4, so outputs",
        "   leave on M2/M3; inputs (A, B, D, CK) are clear of the strips and",
        "   can climb to M4",
        " - a DFRNQNX1 uses M1..M3 across its width inside: no M2/M3 trunk",
        "   over a flop; M4 beside the strips, M5 across",
        " - hops on one layer must not share a row: alternate M2/M3 down the",
        "   column",
        " - no net should run the length of a column: duplicate a driver",
        "   locally instead (CTRL's PWRUP_NB)",
        " - an edge port on a net that already has a via stack on its pin",
        "   takes nostartcut, or the two stacks overlap (cut layers may not",
        "   partially overlap between subcells)",
        " - trunks move by trackN (pitches, relative to the pins), never by",
        "   coordinates",
        "",
        "Rings (REY_PLL_PFD, clean): a net that is not a hop between",
        "neighbours gets its own M5 ring. Inputs connect LEFT on M4 (an input's",
        "via stack leaves M2/M3 pads on the left of the cell, so nothing else",
        "may cross there), outputs connect RIGHT on M3 (right of Y there is",
        "only the VDD strip, whose stack is at the cell's bottom). A flop's D is",
        "on its right, so it connects right on M4. Hops put their trunk LEFT of",
        "the input pins (track-13 from the default): between the pins there is",
        "no room, and right of Y a stub at the A pin's height crosses the cell's",
        "own supply via stack. Connection paths are regexes: anchor them (^DN$,",
        "or DN also matches DN_N). A flop's QN carries the flop's own via on",
        "the pin; take the inverse from an inverter instead."
    ],
